# Design Plan — VBF t1_r1_flash (next-gen BEV sedan battery)
Task: ED ≥ 392.61 Wh/kg; 4C fast charge no plating; T_max ≤ 60°C; overcharge to 4.7 V no thermal runaway.

## Objective decomposition
| Metric | Layer | Threshold | Notes |
- energy_density_wh_kg | stage2 | ≥392.61 | stack-level, electrolyte-excluded contract formula; levers: thickness, porosity, collector thickness, N/P
- plated (4C charge @45°C) | stage3 | false (anode_potential_v min ≥ 0 V) | levers: electrode thickness (thin helps), electrolyte σ/t⁺, negative particle radius, N/P
- T_max_K | stage3 | ≤333.15 (60°C) at 4C charge, 45°C ambient (318.15 K) | only 15 K rise budget → cooling h and internal resistance matter
- triggered (overcharge 4.7 V → TR) | stage3 | false | mechanical via run-tr with cell mass

Trade-offs: ED vs 4C/T_max: thick electrode raises ED but raises overpotential (plating) and heat generation (T_max). Cooling h raises T_max margin at no ED cost (but is a pack-level lever). Electrolyte σ/t⁺ helps 4C at no ED cost. Negative particle size small helps plating.

## Candidate strategy
R1: baseline OKane2022 (system candidate, NMC811/graphite+SiOx) full characterization + Arch-A (thin collectors) + Arch-B (thick positive + thin collectors) ED probes.
After R1: route by failing metric (fallback): ED fail → architecture (thicker, lower porosity); 4C plating fail → electrolyte transport / particle size / thinner electrodes; T_max fail → cooling h / lower DCR; TR fail → cell mass/chemistry.

## Budget
R1: 1 baseline full suite + 2 ED probes; R2: targeted fixes (3-6 sims); R3: final confirmation. Total ~12-18 sims. Zero true compute (real_compute=false).

## Risk & fallback
- Baseline ED below 392.61: possible (OKane2022 is a conservative EV cell ~stock) — thin collectors + thickness push; ceiling assessment after R1.
- 4C plating at end-of-charge likely at high SOC — if baseline fails, σ/t⁺/particle levers; if still fails → reconsider N/P or system.
- T_max with h=10 default will very likely exceed 60°C (hA=0.053 W/K tiny) → cooling h lever (thermal management adjustable, widest interpretation).
- Overcharge TR: 0.5C overcharge to 4.7V generates moderate heat; TR depends on mcp — check mechanically.
- Three-strike plan: if architecture can't reach ED → escalate to Stage 2 (material design: high-voltage cathode or additive); if safety can't be met at ED target → question boundary (h upper limit / system switch).

## References
- OKane2022 parameter set (PyBaMM) — NMC811/graphite+SiOx EV chemistry with cracking + SEI + full thermal geometry.
- "next-gen EV energy density" → Li-ion cell roadmaps (e.g., 300→400 Wh/kg cell-level via high-Ni/Si anodes); domain experience, no precise source.
- Fast-charge plating mitigation: high-conductivity electrolytes, thin electrodes, small particles → domain experience (Yang et al. / Waldmann plating reviews) — mark domain experience.
- Thermal: liquid cooling effective h 100+ W/m²K at pack level — domain experience.

